<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  PawmodoroWidgets — extension entitlements.

  The widget extension is iOS-only (SUPPORTED_PLATFORMS = "iphoneos
  iphonesimulator", and project.pbxproj carries platformFilter = ios on both
  its target dependency and its Embed Foundation Extensions build file), so
  this file is wired up unconditionally:
      CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS = PawmodoroWidgets/PawmodoroWidgets.entitlements

  One key, and it must stay in step with Pawmodoro/iOS/Pawmodoro.entitlements:

    - com.apple.security.application-groups = group.com.pawmodoro
      An App Group is a shared container, and a container is only shared if
      BOTH sides claim it. The app writes "widget.buddy"/"widget.place" into
      UserDefaults(suiteName: "group.com.pawmodoro") from
      TimerEngine.settingsDidChange(); PawmodoroHomeWidget.swift reads
      "widget.buddy" back. Drop this key from either file and the widget falls
      back to "cat" for everyone.

  Nothing else. The extension makes no network calls, touches no files, and
  reads no user data beyond those two mirrored strings.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.com.pawmodoro</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
